WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.833
(pleasant instrumental music)

00:00:13.729 --> 00:00:15.875
- Hi, I'm Hannah, your
friendly neighborhood wine mom

00:00:15.875 --> 00:00:16.999
and if you're anything like me

00:00:16.999 --> 00:00:18.424
you believe a glass of wine at eight PM

00:00:18.424 --> 00:00:19.835
makes you a better mom.

00:00:19.835 --> 00:00:20.931
So don't pour yourself a glass

00:00:20.931 --> 00:00:23.175
because today we have a
really special guest again,

00:00:23.175 --> 00:00:24.404
you might recognize him

00:00:24.404 --> 00:00:26.428
from the last wine pairing video we did.

00:00:26.428 --> 00:00:30.054
Please welcome Christopher
Webb, our fancy wine man.

00:00:30.054 --> 00:00:30.887
- [Christopher] Hi.

00:00:30.887 --> 00:00:32.066
- Hi, welcome back.

00:00:32.066 --> 00:00:33.072
- [Christopher] Do you want me to just--

00:00:33.072 --> 00:00:33.933
- Oh, you can just throw it on the floor.

00:00:33.933 --> 00:00:36.601
So why don't you tell the people
who haven't seen you before

00:00:36.601 --> 00:00:37.710
a little bit about yourself.

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:39.266
- As you said, my name's Christopher Webb.

00:00:39.266 --> 00:00:42.706
I'm a sommelier at a restaurant in Malibu

00:00:42.706 --> 00:00:47.380
and my job is essentially
helping people find the wine

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:49.233
that they're going to
enjoy with their meal.

00:00:49.233 --> 00:00:52.554
- So the last pairing was food and wine

00:00:52.554 --> 00:00:54.080
and I know that's what
you're used to doing.

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:56.749
I wanna try some abstract pairings.

00:00:56.749 --> 00:00:59.163
So tonight we're gonna do wines to pair

00:00:59.163 --> 00:01:01.242
with your kids' crappy behavior.

00:01:01.242 --> 00:01:02.075
- Wow, okay.

00:01:02.075 --> 00:01:02.908
- You think you're up for it?

00:01:02.908 --> 00:01:03.772
- Well, I'll do my best.

00:01:03.772 --> 00:01:05.520
- Okay, let's go.

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:09.687
Okay, so first scenario my
youngest son is about the age

00:01:10.645 --> 00:01:12.774
where it's time to start potty training.

00:01:12.774 --> 00:01:16.416
There would be days where
I'd walk into a room

00:01:16.416 --> 00:01:18.346
and just be like (sniffs)

00:01:18.346 --> 00:01:19.506
where's the crap?

00:01:19.506 --> 00:01:20.885
'Cause there's poop in this room

00:01:20.885 --> 00:01:25.026
and I realized that my
son's choice pooping spot

00:01:25.026 --> 00:01:26.749
was the corner of my closet.

00:01:26.749 --> 00:01:29.996
And that scent just lingers in your house.

00:01:29.996 --> 00:01:32.180
- Like poop-pouri.

00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:33.805
(laughs)

00:01:33.805 --> 00:01:38.164
- So what I'm asking is what
is the best wine to pair

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:40.525
with my son crapping in the closet?

00:01:40.525 --> 00:01:42.669
- Well this is gonna be by
far the strangest pairing

00:01:42.669 --> 00:01:43.916
that I've ever done.

00:01:43.916 --> 00:01:46.842
The first thing that comes
to mind is aromatic whites

00:01:46.842 --> 00:01:49.387
and one of them that
has the strongest aroma

00:01:49.387 --> 00:01:53.862
is called Moschofilero
which is a Greek white wine.

00:01:53.862 --> 00:01:57.195
And the cool thing about Greece wines...

00:01:59.243 --> 00:02:01.133
- Nice, thank you.

00:02:01.133 --> 00:02:05.407
- Smell like rose petals
and lemon, citrus.

00:02:05.407 --> 00:02:07.324
- I smell shit blocker.

00:02:08.969 --> 00:02:10.386
Am I doing this right?

00:02:10.386 --> 00:02:14.047
- Well, at some point you
can actually drink it.

00:02:14.047 --> 00:02:17.467
- Oh, we're doing that, that thing right?

00:02:17.467 --> 00:02:19.467
(slurp)

00:02:21.141 --> 00:02:21.974
- There ya go.

00:02:21.974 --> 00:02:22.807
(slurp)

00:02:22.807 --> 00:02:23.640
That's pretty good.

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:25.603
Does your son really crap in the closet.

00:02:25.603 --> 00:02:28.883
(classical music)

00:02:28.883 --> 00:02:30.536
- Oh yeah.

00:02:30.536 --> 00:02:33.514
So next, because we haven't
gotten personal enough.

00:02:33.514 --> 00:02:37.387
When parents want to have
alone time we call it talking.

00:02:37.387 --> 00:02:38.854
You have to schedule them.

00:02:38.854 --> 00:02:40.086
It's like a huge ordeal.

00:02:40.086 --> 00:02:42.125
Like we will plant the kids on the couch,

00:02:42.125 --> 00:02:43.481
turn on their favorite TV show,

00:02:43.481 --> 00:02:46.424
spread out a smorgasbord of snacks,

00:02:46.424 --> 00:02:48.376
and then it's like alright
let's go, go, go, go go.

00:02:48.376 --> 00:02:49.710
We got 10 minutes, like--

00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:50.543
- No pressure.

00:02:50.543 --> 00:02:54.873
- The four-year-old now, even
though we will lock the door

00:02:54.873 --> 00:02:55.982
he knows how to unlock it.

00:02:55.982 --> 00:02:58.552
So is there a wine that
can restart the romance

00:02:58.552 --> 00:03:00.889
after our son has walked in on us?

00:03:00.889 --> 00:03:03.117
- When I think of romance,

00:03:03.117 --> 00:03:05.813
the first thing that comes
to mind is like champagne

00:03:05.813 --> 00:03:07.258
or sparkling wine.

00:03:07.258 --> 00:03:11.287
Actually one of my
favorites is Franciacorta,

00:03:11.287 --> 00:03:14.787
which is essentially an Italian champagne.

00:03:15.911 --> 00:03:17.646
- Do we need different glasses for this?

00:03:17.646 --> 00:03:19.903
- Well traditionally you
serve a sparkling wine,

00:03:19.903 --> 00:03:21.025
champagne, Franciacorta--

00:03:21.025 --> 00:03:22.942
- In paper cups.

00:03:22.942 --> 00:03:23.775
- Champagne flutes.

00:03:23.775 --> 00:03:24.629
(laughs)

00:03:24.629 --> 00:03:26.984
- These are never used in my house.

00:03:26.984 --> 00:03:31.262
I'm not above drinking
wine out of paper cups.

00:03:31.262 --> 00:03:32.641
Wait, you have more than me.

00:03:32.641 --> 00:03:33.797
- Oh, yeah let's switch.

00:03:33.797 --> 00:03:34.857
- Hold on, okay.

00:03:34.857 --> 00:03:37.636
(classical music)

00:03:37.636 --> 00:03:38.631
(satisfied exclamation)

00:03:38.631 --> 00:03:39.464
- That's nice.

00:03:39.464 --> 00:03:40.991
Maybe like a hint of almond.

00:03:40.991 --> 00:03:42.547
- Almond?

00:03:42.547 --> 00:03:43.380
- Yeah.

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:44.440
- How do you taste that?

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:48.418
How do you like train
your tongue to taste that?

00:03:48.418 --> 00:03:51.852
I mean, when my husband
comes home tonight, hello.

00:03:51.852 --> 00:03:54.240
To Matt, you're gettin' lucky.

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:56.914
Next, there's something
that happened the other day.

00:03:56.914 --> 00:03:59.180
I just didn't quite know
how to deal with it.

00:03:59.180 --> 00:04:02.649
We were in the elevator,
it was me and my oldest son

00:04:02.649 --> 00:04:05.377
who's four and he just talks nonstop

00:04:05.377 --> 00:04:07.152
to anybody who will listen.

00:04:07.152 --> 00:04:09.879
He turns to this woman
who gets on the elevator.

00:04:09.879 --> 00:04:12.265
He looks her dead in the eyes and is like,

00:04:12.265 --> 00:04:14.645
"You know my mom takes big poops."

00:04:14.645 --> 00:04:15.760
(aggravated exclamation)

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:18.605
So is there a wine that's
gonna pair with my child

00:04:18.605 --> 00:04:21.810
over sharing information
with complete strangers?

00:04:21.810 --> 00:04:22.731
- This is gettin' weird.

00:04:22.731 --> 00:04:23.790
(laughs)

00:04:23.790 --> 00:04:27.136
Well this one might be a
stretch, but I'm gonna just say

00:04:27.136 --> 00:04:31.303
that maybe you need to add a
little sweetness in your life.

00:04:32.744 --> 00:04:36.702
I know what I turn to on days like that.

00:04:36.702 --> 00:04:38.462
I love Riesling.

00:04:38.462 --> 00:04:40.503
It's got some really nice qualities to it.

00:04:40.503 --> 00:04:43.221
Traditionally with Riesling
you're going to get

00:04:43.221 --> 00:04:46.638
a lot of like stone fruit and minerality.

00:04:49.909 --> 00:04:52.292
- I just got it all over.

00:04:52.292 --> 00:04:53.853
(happy exclamation)

00:04:53.853 --> 00:04:56.151
It's like a stronger juice.

00:04:56.151 --> 00:04:58.548
But this is really delicious.

00:04:58.548 --> 00:05:02.131
And for the record, I
don't take big poops.

00:05:04.036 --> 00:05:05.832
(smacking)

00:05:05.832 --> 00:05:06.694
Get pumped.

00:05:06.694 --> 00:05:10.970
Next, every parent has a
worst nightmare of parenting.

00:05:10.970 --> 00:05:13.883
That's something like you're
gonna need a code red wine

00:05:13.883 --> 00:05:16.262
on hand that's just like this is it,

00:05:16.262 --> 00:05:18.397
this is what makes me feel better.

00:05:18.397 --> 00:05:20.216
- Like break in case of emergency.

00:05:20.216 --> 00:05:22.535
- Exactly, like a fire extinguisher.

00:05:22.535 --> 00:05:25.095
What is a wine that could pair

00:05:25.095 --> 00:05:26.709
with a parent's worst nightmare?

00:05:26.709 --> 00:05:29.050
- Well, what would be
your worst nightmare?

00:05:29.050 --> 00:05:30.245
- Where do I start?

00:05:30.245 --> 00:05:31.730
Arrive at your destination in the car,

00:05:31.730 --> 00:05:33.287
take the kid out of the car seat,

00:05:33.287 --> 00:05:35.343
smear of poop all over the car seat.

00:05:35.343 --> 00:05:39.724
Bloody noses, lice, the
biting phase, sleep training,

00:05:39.724 --> 00:05:42.584
kids handing you their boogers, Caillou.

00:05:42.584 --> 00:05:43.417
- What's Caillou?

00:05:43.417 --> 00:05:45.045
- Oh, you don't wanna know.

00:05:45.045 --> 00:05:47.130
- Okay, it sounds to me
like you need something

00:05:47.130 --> 00:05:51.912
that's very drinkable, something
that is maybe easy to pair

00:05:51.912 --> 00:05:53.745
with any kind of food.

00:05:54.815 --> 00:05:56.640
- Are you gonna say what
I think you're gonna say?

00:05:56.640 --> 00:05:58.171
Rose!

00:05:58.171 --> 00:05:59.004
- Rose.

00:05:59.004 --> 00:06:00.659
- Rose all day!

00:06:00.659 --> 00:06:02.888
Aka the chug course.

00:06:02.888 --> 00:06:03.721
- No.

00:06:03.721 --> 00:06:04.554
- Cheers.

00:06:10.260 --> 00:06:13.549
Chug, chug, chug, chug, chug, chug.

00:06:13.549 --> 00:06:15.089
You're no fun.

00:06:15.089 --> 00:06:17.251
Last, and I'm saving this for last

00:06:17.251 --> 00:06:19.260
because it truly broke my heart.

00:06:19.260 --> 00:06:21.025
I was out here on the
couch doing some work.

00:06:21.025 --> 00:06:25.410
My son was in his room and
he had gotten into my purse

00:06:25.410 --> 00:06:27.252
and emptied my makeup bag

00:06:27.252 --> 00:06:29.036
and took my really expensive foundation,

00:06:29.036 --> 00:06:30.227
which is the last thing

00:06:30.227 --> 00:06:32.561
that I actually spend money on for myself,

00:06:32.561 --> 00:06:36.821
and he had squeezed the entire
bottle out onto his floor

00:06:36.821 --> 00:06:39.567
and was finger painting in it, really?

00:06:39.567 --> 00:06:42.449
So is there a wine that
will pair with the fact

00:06:42.449 --> 00:06:46.043
that your kids ruin every
nice thing you have?

00:06:46.043 --> 00:06:48.836
- Well it sounds like you're
looking for inexpensive wine.

00:06:48.836 --> 00:06:51.264
I think the least expensive
wine I can think of

00:06:51.264 --> 00:06:52.792
is boxed wine.

00:06:52.792 --> 00:06:53.769
- Do you have some?

00:06:53.769 --> 00:06:56.558
- No, I mean nothing against it,

00:06:56.558 --> 00:06:58.416
I just, I would never--

00:06:58.416 --> 00:07:02.583
- I feel like I have some,
I probably do, hold on.

00:07:03.615 --> 00:07:05.615
Okay, I have a surprise.

00:07:08.123 --> 00:07:11.728
(ripping and tearing)

00:07:11.728 --> 00:07:14.892
- I don't think you're supposed
to tear the whole thing off.

00:07:14.892 --> 00:07:16.124
(laughs)

00:07:16.124 --> 00:07:17.534
Hold on, it's like a waterbed.

00:07:17.534 --> 00:07:19.242
(sloshing)

00:07:19.242 --> 00:07:20.700
Should we just pour it into our mouths

00:07:20.700 --> 00:07:22.607
or pour it into a glass?

00:07:22.607 --> 00:07:24.400
- I don't see the difference really.

00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:27.150
- Oh this looks nice, nice color.

00:07:28.874 --> 00:07:30.207
Should we swirl?

00:07:32.076 --> 00:07:34.463
Do you wanna chug this one too?

00:07:34.463 --> 00:07:37.463
- I don't even wanna drink this one.

00:07:39.006 --> 00:07:43.204
- Hey fancy wine man, what
are the notes of this?

00:07:43.204 --> 00:07:44.784
- I feel like

00:07:44.784 --> 00:07:47.605
that's like what the inside
of a glow stick tastes like.

00:07:47.605 --> 00:07:50.855
- Yeah no, I don't need new foundation.

00:07:51.871 --> 00:07:53.936
Do you wanna take this home?

00:07:53.936 --> 00:07:55.179
- Nah, I'm good.

00:07:55.179 --> 00:07:56.328
- So that's all I got for today.

00:07:56.328 --> 00:07:58.323
I'm Hannah, your friendly
neighborhood wine mom.

00:07:58.323 --> 00:08:00.599
Just wanna remind everyone
that we had a lot of fun

00:08:00.599 --> 00:08:02.579
pairing wines with kids' crappy behaviors

00:08:02.579 --> 00:08:05.569
but we're not promoting wine
as a crutch for motherhood.

00:08:05.569 --> 00:08:07.937
Everything in moderation,
everything in good fun.

00:08:07.937 --> 00:08:10.440
Thank you so much to Chris
for coming on the show again.

00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:12.809
If you want to find
him in the interwebs...

00:08:12.809 --> 00:08:14.777
- @topherwebb on Twitter.

00:08:14.777 --> 00:08:16.133
- On Twitter?

00:08:16.133 --> 00:08:16.966
- Twitter.

00:08:16.966 --> 00:08:18.876
- So I really wanna see your
worst parenting nightmares

00:08:18.876 --> 00:08:20.105
in the comments.

00:08:20.105 --> 00:08:22.454
Share if you've experienced
any of these other things

00:08:22.454 --> 00:08:23.892
that I've talked about.

00:08:23.892 --> 00:08:24.969
And as always, if you have a topic

00:08:24.969 --> 00:08:26.796
that you really want to hear more about,

00:08:26.796 --> 00:08:28.060
leave that in the comments as well

00:08:28.060 --> 00:08:29.943
because I love doing
what you guys wanna see.

00:08:29.943 --> 00:08:30.776
Until next time.

00:08:30.776 --> 00:08:33.295
(classical music)

00:08:33.295 --> 00:08:35.295
(belch)

00:08:36.762 --> 00:08:40.050
- Are you jealous, you can't burp.

00:08:40.050 --> 00:08:40.883
- No.

00:08:40.883 --> 00:08:42.004
(laughs)

